{{/* @dot donseba/go-webthings-docs/internal/website.DocsArticleData */}}
<article class="grid max-w-5xl gap-6">
    {{ template "hero.gohtml" . }}

<h2>Append keys to the POT file</h2>
<pre><code>tr := translator.NewTranslator("translations", "templates")
if err := tr.CheckMissingTranslations(); err != nil { return err }</code></pre>
<p><code>CheckMissingTranslations</code> scans the <code>.gohtml</code> files below the template directory and appends the keys that are not yet in <code>translations/translations.pot</code>: first in the order they appear in the templates, then the keys recorded at runtime, sorted. When the POT file does not exist yet, it is created with a gettext header first; the translations directory must exist. It returns the errors of every key it could not add, joined. A translator made with <code>New</code> has no template directory: call <code>SetTemplateDir</code> first.</p>
<p>It only appends. To write the whole POT file with source references, and to check what each language still misses, use the <a href="{{ basePath }}/extract" hx-get="{{ basePath }}/extract" hx-target="#content" hx-push-url="true">extract package</a>.</p>
<h2>Supported template syntax</h2>
<pre><code>{{"{{"}} tl .Loc "Welcome" }}
{{"{{"}} tl localizer "Hello, %s" .Name }}
{{"{{"}} $loc := .Loc }}
{{"{{"}} tn $loc "message" "messages" .Count }}
{{"{{"}} ctl $loc "navigation" "Home" }}
{{"{{"}} if eq (tl $loc "Ready") "Ready" }}...{{"{{"}} end }}</code></pre>
<p>The parser walks template definitions, actions and nested expressions. It recognizes <code>tl</code>, <code>tn</code>, <code>ctl</code> and <code>ctn</code> with literal key/context arguments; the localizer can be a field, variable, or helper. Application helper functions need not be registered just to scan the files.</p>
<h2>What static extraction skips</h2>
<p>Comments, dynamic keys, Go source and struct tags are not extracted. For example, <code>tl .Loc .ErrorKey</code> is discovered only when the runtime lookup occurs with recording on. Empty keys are left out. Malformed templates return an error naming the source file, and no key of that scan is kept. Escaped quotes and newlines are preserved as PO escapes.</p>
<h2>Recording keys at runtime</h2>
<p>Lookups also record keys they have not seen, including keys constructed in Go code, and append them to the POT file. An empty key is not recorded. A translator made with <code>NewTranslator</code> records by default; <code>New</code> and <code>Untranslated</code> record nothing unless you call <code>SetRecordMissing(true)</code>. Turn recording off where serving requests must never write to disk:</p>
<pre><code>tr.SetRecordMissing(false)</code></pre>
<p>With recording off, lookups only translate and never read the POT file; <code>CheckMissingTranslations</code> and <code>ScanFiles</code> still extract keys when you call them. <code>RecordMissing()</code> reports the setting. The POT file is read the first time it is needed; <code>SetTranslationsDir</code> and <code>SetPotFile</code> take effect for the next key recorded.</p>
<p>A lookup has no error to return, so errors of runtime recording, such as a POT file that cannot be written, are logged with <code>log/slog</code>.</p>
<h2>A catalogue workflow</h2>
<ol><li>Extract during development or asset preparation.</li><li>Merge new source entries into each PO catalogue using your gettext editor or tooling, such as “Translation → Update from POT File” in Poedit.</li><li>Translate the entries and check placeholders and plural forms.</li><li>Load the reviewed PO files at application startup.</li></ol>
<p>Runtime lookup discovery is serialized, but each translator instance owns its lock. Use one process to update a shared POT file; for several application instances, give discovery separate writable storage or manage extraction as a build step. <code>ScanFiles(root)</code> extracts and remembers the keys of the templates below another root; the next <code>CheckMissingTranslations()</code> appends them too.</p>
</article>
